        "email": "gaireview@linuxhacker.ru",
        "username": "aireview",
        "status": "Contact Oleg Drokin (green@whamcloud.com) with any questions on this account"
      },
      "date": "2026-07-07 06:14:26.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 1:\n\nExperimental feature testing in progress, please pay attention to the comments\n\nThe configure logic change itself looks correct: HAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT is now defined only when modules are disabled, and both diff hunks are explained by the commit message.\n\nThis fixes a real build-configuration bug (JIRA LU-20419 is filed as a Bug), so it should carry a Fixes: tag pointing at the commit that introduced the unconditional AC_DEFINE in the AC_ARG_ENABLE action-if-given branch:\n\n    Fixes: d963e66f609c (\"LU-13903 uapi: fixup UAPI headers for native Linux client.\")\n\nThat commit added `[ AC_DEFINE(HAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT, 1, ...) ]` as the action-if-given, which runs for --enable-modules too, leaving the macro defined when modules are enabled.",
      "accounts_in_message": [],
      "_revision_number": 1
    },
