        "subject": "LU-20419 build: Make --enable-modules work correctly",
        "message": "LU-20419 build: Make --enable-modules work correctly\n\nIf explicit \"--enable-modules\" is given as input to\nconfigure, it still leaves HAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT\ndefined. The behavior of default action and\n\"--enable-modules\" should be same. It should not define\nHAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT. Only --disable-modules should\ndefine HAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT\n\nAlso, improve configure --help message for --disable-modules\n\nBefore patch\n=============\n./configure --enable-modules\n...\ncat config.log | grep NATIVE\ndefine HAVE_NATIVE_LINUX_CLIENT 1\n...\n\nAfter patch\n=============\n./configure --enable-modules\n...\ncat config.log | grep NATIVE | wc -l\n0\n\nFixes: d963e66f6 (\"LU-13903 uapi: fixup UAPI headers for native Linux client.\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nSigned-off-by: Arshad Hussain <arshad.hussain@aeoncomputing.com>\nChange-Id: Ie4e52b9a03b7281e66cd68e595ca16cb1f2db268\n"
      },
